=== SIGNATURE ===
arrow_move(start_ad, arrow, [steps], [board_rng], [push_mode])

=== COMMENT ===
Moves a start address (numeric or A1) 'steps' (default 1) in an arrow direction (arrow glyph, its numeric equivalent, or a letter code like "R"/"UL"), bounded by board_rng (default whole sheet). Returns a NUMERIC address. Out of bounds, push_mode: 0 = report "oob;<row>;<col>" with the intended (possibly zero/negative) coordinates (default), 1 = stop at edge, -1 = stay at start.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(start_ad, arrow, [steps], [board_rng], [push_mode],
  LET(
    step_n, IF(ISOMITTED(steps), 1, steps),
    mode, IF(ISOMITTED(push_mode), 0, push_mode),
    start_num, num_ad(start_ad),
    start_row, INT(start_num / 1000000),
    start_col, MOD(start_num, 1000000),
    arr_norm, z_dir_to_arrow(arrow),
    d_row, SWITCH(arr_norm, "←", 0, "↖", -1, "↗", -1, "→", 0, "↙", 1, "↓", 1, "↘", 1, "↑", -1),
    d_col, SWITCH(arr_norm, "←", -1, "↖", -1, "↗", 1, "→", 1, "↙", -1, "↓", 0, "↘", 1, "↑", 0),
    row_min, IF(ISOMITTED(board_rng), 1, MIN(ROW(board_rng))),
    row_max, IF(ISOMITTED(board_rng), 1048576, MAX(ROW(board_rng))),
    col_min, IF(ISOMITTED(board_rng), 1, MIN(COLUMN(board_rng))),
    col_max, IF(ISOMITTED(board_rng), 16384, MAX(COLUMN(board_rng))),
    try_row, start_row + d_row * step_n,
    try_col, start_col + d_col * step_n,
    push_row, MIN(MAX(try_row, row_min), row_max),
    push_col, MIN(MAX(try_col, col_min), col_max),
    oob, OR(try_row <> push_row, try_col <> push_col),
    IF(oob,
      SWITCH(mode,
        1, 1000000 * push_row + push_col,
        0, "oob;" & try_row & ";" & try_col,
        -1, 1000000 * start_row + start_col,
        "oob;" & try_row & ";" & try_col),
      1000000 * try_row + try_col)
  )
)

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Moves an address a number of steps in an arrow direction, constrained to a board. Computes in numeric-address space and RETURNS A NUMERIC address (use str_ad for the final A1 answer).

Arguments:
  start_ad    - starting cell as a numeric address or an A1 string (coerced with num_ad).
  arrow       - direction as a standard arrow (↑↓←→↖↗↙↘), its numeric equivalent (1, -1000000, ...), or a letter code (U D L R UL UR DL DR).
  [steps]     - number of steps (default 1).
  [board_rng] - bounding range (default whole sheet).
  [push_mode] - out-of-bounds behavior:
                  0 = report "oob" (default) - returns the string "oob;<row>;<col>"
                      where row/col are the INTENDED coordinates, kept even when
                      zero or negative so you can see where the move pointed.
                  1 = stop at edge - clamp to the nearest in-bounds cell.
                 -1 = stay at start - return the starting address unchanged.

Returns:
  The destination as a numeric address (mode 1 clamps to the edge, mode -1 stays
  put), or the string "oob;<row>;<col>" under the default mode 0. In the oob
  string, row and col are the intended landing coordinates (which may be 0 or
  negative), reported on both axes even if only one is out of bounds.

Example:
  arrow_move("A1", "→", 3)       -> 1000004     (in bounds; str_ad -> "D1")
  arrow_move("B1", "↖", 2)       -> "oob;-1;0"  (row 1-2=-1, col 2-2=0, both off)
  arrow_move("B1", "↖", 2, , 1)  -> 1000001     (stop at edge -> A1)
  arrow_move("B1", "↖", 2, , -1) -> 1000002     (stay at start -> B1)
